<title>CZECH REPUBLIC: CZECH SEPAP CONSOL 9MO NET FALLS - CAS.</title>
<headline>CZECH SEPAP CONSOL 9MO NET FALLS - CAS.</headline>
<dateline>PRAGUE 1996-11-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>Consolidated results, calculated</p>
<p>according to Czech accounting standards (CAS), for nine-month</p>
<p>period ending September 30, 1996 compared to full year 1995</p>
<p>results: (in millions of crowns)</p>
<p> Net profit	    194.224    vs    644.480</p>
<p> Operational profit  400.790    vs  1,262.436</p>
<p> Pre-tax profit	164.265    vs    988.384</p>
<p> Revenues from the</p>
<p>  sale of goods	 12.062    vs     18.925</p>
<p> Revenues from sales of own products</p>
<p>  and services	4,185.071   vs  7,133.871</p>
<p> Revenues from sales</p>
<p> of investment property</p>
<p>  and materials	  33,461   vs     59.181</p>
<p>Note. Full company name is Sepap Group a.s., a paper and</p>
<p>forest products concern. Coparative figures for January-</p>
<p>September 1995 were not immediately available. Its two main</p>
<p>shareholders are Daventree Ltd, controlled by Bahamas-based</p>
<p>investor Michael Dingman (48 percent), and Swedish forestry</p>
<p>concern Assidoman AS (39 percent).</p>
<p>-- Prague Newsroom, 42-2-2423-0003</p>
</text>
